      "excerpt": "Malawi stunned Ghana 2-1 to reach the WAFCON 2026 semi-finals and qualify for the FIFA Women\u2019s World Cup Brazil 2027. Ghana bettors should explore betting tips and odds.",
      "body": "Malawi\u2019s stunning 2-1 victory over Ghana in the Women\u2019s Africa Cup of Nations (WAFCON) 2026 quarter-finals has sent shockwaves through Ghanaian football. This historic win not only secured Malawi\u2019s place in the semi-finals but also booked their first-ever ticket to the FIFA Women\u2019s World Cup Brazil 2027. For Ghanaian bettors, this result is a pivotal moment to reassess betting strategies and market expectations as the tournament progresses.\n\nThe defeat was a tough blow for Ghana\u2019s Black Queens, who entered the match as favourites given their rich history and experience in African women\u2019s football. However, Malawi\u2019s debutant Scorchers showed remarkable resilience and tactical discipline to overturn expectations. This article breaks down the implications of this result for Ghana\u2019s betting market, compares odds from top Ghanaian bookmakers, and offers strategic betting tips tailored for Ghanaian punters.\n\n## Malawi\u2019s Historic Win and What It Means for Ghanaian Bettors\n\nMalawi\u2019s 2-1 win over Ghana was a classic underdog story. The Scorchers, making their WAFCON debut, stunned the defending champions and Ghana\u2019s passionate home crowd. This victory marks a milestone for Malawi but also signals a potential shift in the competitive landscape of African women\u2019s football.\n\nFor bettors in Ghana, this upset means the market is more volatile than expected. The Black Queens\u2019 early exit opens up new betting opportunities in the semi-finals and beyond, especially for markets involving Malawi and other emerging teams. Ghanaian bettors should watch how bookmakers adjust odds for the remaining teams and consider value bets on underdogs who have shown they can upset favourites.\n\n## Comparing Odds: Sportybet Ghana vs Betway Ghana\n\nWhen it comes to betting on WAFCON 2026 matches, Ghanaian punters have access to several licensed bookmakers regulated by the Gaming Commission of Ghana (GCA). Two of t